        "description": "Blackwell vLLM-Omni profile for cosmos3_nano_t2i_720p using cuDNN attention.",
        "notes": "Blackwell attention choice, measured on this box 2026-09-12. FLASH_ATTN is a Hopper-only precompiled kernel -- vLLM-Omni refuses it on sm_100 with 'FLASH_ATTN was explicitly selected but is unsupported'. FLASHINFER_ATTN starts but dies under torch.compile on dynamic shapes (`AsPythonConstantNotImplementedError: SymNodeVariable() is not a constant` in the FlashInfer backend's _ensure_plan), observed on qwen-image and cosmos3 t2v; it is fine for the static image cases (zimage, flux), which are deliberately left on it. CUDNN_ATTN is exact softmax, the same precision class as the kernels the other frameworks run here, measured at 2.741s on qwen-image (vs TRTLLM_ATTN 3.274s) and already the backend minimax-h3 serves with on this box. Also drops --stage-configs-path: vLLM-Omni 0.29 rejects it outright (`stage_configs_path is no longer supported; use deploy_config instead`), and upstream's own cosmos3 deploy file says the T2I/video checkpoints must keep the default single-stage diffusion fallback -- so cfg-parallel and guardrails move to the first-class flags rather than to a new YAML. The old YAML also pinned enforce_eager, which silently ran this competitor compile-off against the policy.",
